cells:
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "Problem : aga padta ja raha ha picha ka bhulta ja raha ha           \r

      Solution : Revise notes,make project ,write blog ,make youtube videos "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "Today we study window functions which is extreamly very
      important       \r

      yadi aap koi bhi roadmap deko sql ka to became data analyst or data
      scientist ki apko kiya kiya sikna chaya tho windows functions ka upar
      emphaises karega .             \r

      Because analyatics perspective sa you do a lot of things in window
      functions        \r

      our goal is ki aap sara windows functions siko . aor us sa questions ko
      solve kar paho."
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "# What are Windows functions "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "Windows functions are very similar to grouby lakin thodi si
      functionality alag hoti ha wahi huma aaj padna ha "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "Windows function Sql ma ek type ka analytical function hota ha "
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "![alt
      text](https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:4800/format:webp/1*JXIS2GtqVz\
      rOQv4Tvn8yPA.png)"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: Window functions are powerful tools in SQL that allow you to perform
      calculations across a subset of rows related to the current row, without
      collapsing the data into a single result set. Unlike aggregate functions
      like SUM() or COUNT(), which return a single value for a group of rows,
      window functions retain the individual rows while adding additional
      analytical insights.
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: A window function performs a calculation across a set of rows (called a
      window) defined by a PARTITION BY clause. This "window" can be the entire
      dataset or a subset of it. The results of window functions are returned
      for each row in the result set.
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "```javascript\r

      function_name(expression) OVER (\r

      \    [PARTITION BY column_name(s)]\r

      \    [ORDER BY column_name(s)]\r

      )\r

      ```"
    metadata: {}
